        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pea protein isolate is the most practical dairy-free protein for most people. It is cheap, high in protein per calorie, easy to digest and good enough on amino acids to support real muscle gain, provided you take about 30 to 35 g per shake rather than a whey-sized scoop.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Spend your attention on two things: documentation and dose. Buy a brand that shows its heavy-metal testing or holds a certification you can confirm in the certifier's database, choose vanilla or unflavored for daily use, and compare products on cost per 25 g of protein rather than price per tub. Do that and the cheapest pea isolate on the shelf can be one of the best value proteins you buy.
